  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th and a Phase One budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The team has expanded to include five new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with onboarding sessions held in April, September, and for new hires Mike Chen and Lisa Ray. Key milestones include reaching the first major milestone ahead of schedule with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype, and achieving a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% increase in efficiency through AI algorithms, and the project is currently in a phase of gathering innovative ideas to enhance data visualization tools. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective from January next year. Updates and next steps are being discussed, with detailed reports and status reviews planned for meetings on November 20th and August 5th."
